`git diff master --stat -- web/static/js/insights.js
web/static/js/insights-trends-cap.test.cjs web/templates/` confirms the only
change vs master is insights.js (+98/-5); templates untouched. The fix
(ruling TC-2026-09-08b): `trendsChartRaw` now stores the endpoint payload
WITHOUT markers; `renderTrendsChart()` calls `insightChartMarkers()` (reads
`--accent` custom property + `.dark` class) fresh on every render and
applies it to the filtered copy, so every table-driven re-render (cap,
toggle, sort, HTMX swap) repaints with the CURRENT theme, not a value baked
in at fetch time.

