OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking):
- Trace 1's diagonal-hatch fill means a raw center-pixel sample can land in
  a gap (near-background) rather than the stroke; the histogram method
  used here (most-frequent non-background colour) is the correct way to
  pixel-audit a patterned Plotly bar and is noted here for future chart
  contrast probes on this codebase.
- The endpoint (`/insights/trends/chart`) itself returns a per-point
  marker.color array (red/green/gray keyed to increase/decrease) on
  trace 0; `renderTrendsChart()` unconditionally overwrites
  `trace.marker` with the flat `insightChartMarkers()` object, discarding
  that per-point array. This is PRE-EXISTING (master's
  `htmx:afterRequest` handler already did
  `data.data.forEach((trace,i)=>{trace.marker=markers[i]})` before TC1;
  confirmed via `git diff master -- web/static/js/insights.js`, which
  shows this line only moved into `renderTrendsChart()`, not introduced).
  Out of TC1's scope — not a FAIL, flagged for the backlog only.
- The finding-B fix from ruling TC-2026-09-08b (12-category height=576
  test case) is in the test file per the manifest but was not re-executed
  here (`checker-tests`'/`checker-second`'s lane, not a11y's); a11y's
  concern (visual contrast/parity) is fully covered above.

